# rig.conf.example — copy to rig.conf and edit for your build, then the rig auto-loads it.
#   cp rig.conf.example rig.conf   &&   $EDITOR rig.conf   &&   bin/rig doctor
# Every key is listed here; commented-out keys show their default. The file is sourced by bash, so quote
# values with spaces. A variable already set in the environment when the rig is sourced wins over the
# same key here (e.g. `RIG_BUILD=/other/build bin/rig run scenarios/example`).
# lib/rig.sh sources ../rig.conf automatically; point elsewhere with RIG_CONF=/path/to/rig.conf.
# `bin/rig doctor` checks every key below and names the key in each problem it reports.

# --- Your build (REQUIRED) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory that contains the compiled client + dedicated-server binaries and the client's local
# openmw.cfg. The rig only reads this directory.
RIG_BUILD=$HOME/your-build

# Binary + config filenames inside RIG_BUILD. Defaults are TES3MP's; set yours if it rebranded.
# RIG_SERVER_CFG is the server's default config next to its binary; the rig never edits it — each run
# gets its own tes3mp-server.cfg (server home + master announce) through the server's XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
RIG_CLIENT_BIN=tes3mp
RIG_SERVER_BIN=tes3mp-server
RIG_SERVER_CFG=tes3mp-server-default.cfg

# Server-side Lua scripts (TES3MP CoreScripts or your fork's). Runs that build a work copy
# (rig_corescripts_overlay) only read this clone; server state and test hooks go into the copy.
RIG_CORESCRIPTS=$HOME/CoreScripts

# Master-server announce. Each run's server config turns it OFF (there is no master in a test env, and
# announcing makes shutdown block ~10s on the deregister). Set 1 to leave the build's setting.
# RIG_MASTER_ANNOUNCE=0

# 0.47-era clients do not auto-load builtin.omwscripts; set 0 so requiredDataFiles.json does not list it.
# RIG_RDF_BUILTIN=1

# --- Content profiles -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One profile per content set on this machine; a test selects one by name (rig_use_content <name>).
#   RIG_CONTENT_<name>_DATA      data directory (required)
#   RIG_CONTENT_<name>_ARCHIVES  .bsa files under DATA, loaded as fallback-archive= (optional)
#   RIG_CONTENT_<name>_FILES     content files under DATA, in load order (required)
# See docs/WRITING-SCENARIOS.md §4.
# Free OpenMW example-suite (git clone --depth 1 https://gitlab.com/OpenMW/example-suite); the worked
# example (bin/rig run scenarios/example) needs this profile.
RIG_CONTENT_example_DATA=$HOME/example-suite/game_template/data
RIG_CONTENT_example_FILES="template.omwgame"
# Morrowind with both expansions, if you own it (commercial data — keep tests built on it out of a
# public repo; scenarios/local/ is gitignored for that).
# RIG_CONTENT_mw_DATA="$HOME/morrowind/Data Files"
# RIG_CONTENT_mw_ARCHIVES="Morrowind.bsa Tribunal.bsa Bloodmoon.bsa"
# RIG_CONTENT_mw_FILES="Morrowind.esm Tribunal.esm Bloodmoon.esm"

# Where the client content block is written. profile (default): into each client's isolated profile
# openmw.cfg; the build's openmw.cfg must then carry no content= lines. build: between '# RIG-CONTENT'
# markers in $RIG_BUILD/openmw.cfg, stripped at cleanup — only for a client that reads no user
# openmw.cfg; a killed run leaves the block behind.
# RIG_CONTENT_TARGET=profile

# --- Runs -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parent of the per-run directories (rig_run_dir): server log + run-scoped server config, the
# CoreScripts work copy, client logs, shots/, review/. Default: runs/ in this repo (gitignored).
# RIG_RUNS=$HOME/headless-mp-rig/runs
# 1 = keep the CoreScripts work copy in the run dir after the run (post-mortem); default removes it.
# RIG_KEEP_WORK=0
# Where `bin/rig run --tag T` / `--all` look for scenario dirs when none is named (space-separated).
# RIG_SCENARIOS=$HOME/headless-mp-rig/scenarios
# A label for your build, recorded in each run's env.txt. Default: sha256 prefix of the client binary.
# RIG_BUILD_ID=

# --- Headless environment ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# One Xvfb display per client (see docs/WRITING-SCENARIOS.md "one display per client"). The window
# geometry math (centre 640,360) and every click/crop coordinate assume the 1280x720 screen; doctor
# refuses another size unless RIG_GEOM_UNCHECKED=1.
RIG_DISPLAY=:99
RIG_DISPLAY2=:100
RIG_DISPLAY3=:101
RIG_SCREEN=1280x720x24
# RIG_GEOM_UNCHECKED=0

# Isolated client profiles (XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME per client), wiped at each client start.
# RIG_PROFILE=/tmp/mp-rig-profile
# RIG_PROFILE2=/tmp/mp-rig-profile2
# RIG_PROFILE3=/tmp/mp-rig-profile3
# Optional settings.cfg copied into every fresh profile (model remaps etc.).
# RIG_SETTINGS_SRC=
# Default capture() output dir when a test does not pass one.
# RIG_SHOTDIR=/tmp/mp-rig-shots

# OPTIONAL: a Release-built MyGUI shared lib dir to LD_LIBRARY_PATH-shadow a broken distro MyGUI that
# renders no UI (Debian's libmyguiengine3debian1, built without CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE — see
# docs/WRITING-SCENARIOS.md "invisible UI"). Empty = use the distro MyGUI; never auto-detected.
# RIG_MYGUI_FIXED=

# --- Timeouts (raise on slow / software-GL boxes; these are caps, the happy path is event-gated) --
RIG_WORLD_LOAD=35        # blind world-load fallback (software GL is slow — don't shrink casually)
RIG_BOOT_CAP=75          # max secs to see the client boot milestone before proceeding
RIG_WIGGLE_INTERVAL=20   # idle-wiggler period; MUST stay < the engine's 30s fVanityDelay
# RIG_SERVER_LOAD=3      # secs to let the server bind its port
# RIG_BOOT_SETTLE=6      # settle after the boot milestone (milestone -> name box drawn)
# RIG_CHARGEN_PWBOX=4    # secs for the "create password" box after the name
# RIG_CHARGEN_DLG=5      # secs for each chargen dialog to render
# RIG_LOGIN_CAP=30       # scenario `login`: secs to see the server log the player in (fresh: x3)

# --- Scenario input -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The client's chat-window toggle key (scenario verb `hidechat`); F2 in some builds.
# RIG_CHAT_KEY=F6

# --- Reference binding (normally set per scenario by the test, not here) -------------------------
# Older consumers export these before sourcing lib/compare.sh / lib/logcheck.sh; new tests call
# compare_set_refs / logcheck_set_refs instead. Review dirs default to <run dir>/review.
# RIG_REF_DIR=   RIG_REF_MANIFEST=   RIG_REVIEW_DIR=
# RIG_LOG_REF_DIR=   RIG_LOG_REVIEW_DIR=   RIG_LOG_MARKERS=
# RIG_DEFAULT_METRIC=RMSE   RIG_DEFAULT_THRESHOLD=0.05   RIG_DEFAULT_FUZZ=-
